---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Under the Rod — Daf Yomi Game: Bekhorot 21"
  description="Bekhorot 21: open the four gates Rabbi Shimon's kid might use to reach the tithe pen, play the Gemara's mnemonic tiles in a tug-of-war between the firstborn and the sacrifices, pick the right expert to read a tinuf, and decode what a silent seller's silence means for Rav, Shmuel and Rabbi Yoḥanan."
>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link
    rel="stylesheet"
    href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Frank+Ruhl+Libre:wght@400;500;700;900&display=swap"
  />

  <main class="frank min-h-screen bg-[#0f1613] !text-[#e6ece4]">
    <!-- ============ Hero ============ -->
    <header class="px-4 pt-12 pb-8">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
        <p class="text-sm !text-[#94a69c]">
          <a href="/daf" class="underline decoration-[#35473e] hover:!text-[#e3ae5c]">Daf Yomi Arcade</a>, Bekhorot 21, 9 October 2026
        </p>
        <h1 class="mt-3 text-5xl font-black leading-[1.05] sm:text-6xl">Under the Rod</h1>
        <p class="mt-3 text-2xl !text-[#e3ae5c]" dir="rtl" lang="he">כֹּל אֲשֶׁר יַעֲבֹר תַּחַת הַשָּׁבֶט</p>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-xl text-lg leading-relaxed !text-[#cbd6cd]">
          Once a year the herd files out of a pen through a narrow gate, and every tenth animal is marked with the rod as
          <em>ma'aser</em>, the animal tithe. Today's daf asks which kids get into that pen, and whether the tithe
          behaves like a firstborn or like an ordinary sacrifice. Then it hands the case to a shepherd and goes to market,
          where a seller keeps quiet and three Amoraim read his silence three different ways.
        </p>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 600 100" class="mt-6 w-full" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M10 88 H590" stroke="#35473e" stroke-width="2" />
          <g stroke="#5f7a6b" stroke-width="3">
            <path d="M60 88 V44 M110 88 V44 M160 88 V44 M210 88 V44 M300 88 V44 M350 88 V44" />
            <path d="M56 56 H214 M56 72 H214 M296 56 H354 M296 72 H354" />
          </g>
          <path d="M226 20 L292 52" stroke="#e3ae5c" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round" />
          <circle cx="292" cy="54" r="4" fill="#c4553f" />
          <g fill="#cbd6cd">
            <ellipse cx="254" cy="74" rx="18" ry="9" /><circle cx="272" cy="66" r="6" />
            <rect x="242" y="80" width="3" height="8" /><rect x="262" y="80" width="3" height="8" />
          </g>
          <g fill="#7fae98" opacity="0.8">
            <ellipse cx="420" cy="74" rx="16" ry="8" /><circle cx="436" cy="67" r="5.5" />
            <ellipse cx="480" cy="76" rx="16" ry="8" /><circle cx="496" cy="69" r="5.5" />
            <ellipse cx="540" cy="74" rx="16" ry="8" /><circle cx="556" cy="67" r="5.5" />
          </g>
          <text x="135" y="36" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" fill="#94a69c">the pen</text>
          <text x="260" y="14" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" fill="#e3ae5c">the tenth</text>
        </svg>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm !text-[#94a69c]" aria-live="polite">Score: <span id="tally"></span></p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 pb-20">
      <!-- ============ Part I: gates ============ -->
      <section class="border-t border-[#2a3a32] pt-8" aria-labelledby="p1">
        <h2 id="p1" class="text-3xl font-bold">I. Four gates to the pen</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed !text-[#cbd6cd]">
          A baraita has Rabbi Shimon say: "I saw a single kid that yielded a tithe <em>within its first year</em>." Its daughters
          had a <em>tinuf</em>, a murky discharge, around the start of their seventh month. The first tanna doesn't add
          "within its first year". So what do they disagree about? The Gemara offers four answers (21a:2–5), and each one opens a
          different gate for Rabbi Shimon's kids while the first tanna keeps it shut. Each round shows the Gemara's own words.
          Tap the gate they name. Watch what happens to the gate from the round before: <em>ve-i ba'it eima</em>, "if you like, say
          everyone agrees on that one".
        </p>
        <div id="gateboard" class="mt-5 grid grid-cols-2 gap-2 sm:grid-cols-4"></div>
        <div id="gates" class="mt-5 space-y-5"></div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ Part II: tug ============ -->
      <section class="mt-12 border-t border-[#2a3a32] pt-8" aria-labelledby="p2">
        <h2 id="p2" class="text-3xl font-bold">II. Firstborn or sacrifice?</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed !text-[#cbd6cd]">
          Rabbi Shimon's fourth gate has a source. Rabbi Shimon ben Yehuda reports in his name that a kid "before its time",
          not yet eight days old, enters the pen: "just as a firstborn is holy before its time and offered after its time, so too"
          (21b:1). But why compare the tithe to the firstborn? Ordinary sacrifices can't be consecrated before their time at all.
          The Gemara answers with two strings of mnemonic words. Play each tile to the side it pulls the tithe toward, and throw
          out the tiles that aren't true.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-5 card">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-sm font-bold">
            <span class="!text-[#e3ae5c]">← בְּכוֹר firstborn</span>
            <span class="!text-[#7fc4b0]">sacrifices קֳדָשִׁים →</span>
          </div>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 400 46" class="mt-2 w-full" role="img" aria-label="Rope position">
            <line x1="10" y1="23" x2="390" y2="23" stroke="#5f7a6b" stroke-width="4" stroke-dasharray="2 6" />
            <line x1="200" y1="6" x2="200" y2="40" stroke="#35473e" stroke-width="2" />
            <g id="knot" class="knot" style="transform: translateX(0px)">
              <circle cx="200" cy="23" r="13" fill="#e6ece4" />
              <text x="200" y="28" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" fill="#0f1613" font-weight="700">מעשר</text>
            </g>
          </svg>
          <p id="tugcount" class="mt-1 text-center text-sm !text-[#94a69c]"></p>
        </div>
        <div id="tiles" class="mt-4 space-y-2"></div>
        <div id="bridge" class="mt-5 space-y-5"></div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ Part III: shepherd ============ -->
      <section class="mt-12 border-t border-[#2a3a32] pt-8" aria-labelledby="p3">
        <h2 id="p3" class="text-3xl font-bold">III. Show it to a ḥakham</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed !text-[#cbd6cd]">
          The mishna said a <em>tinuf</em> counts as a birth and exempts the next offspring from firstborn status. What does one look
          like, and who can tell (21b:4–5)?
        </p>
        <div id="shep" class="mt-5 space-y-5"></div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ Part IV: silent seller ============ -->
      <section class="mt-12 border-t border-[#2a3a32] pt-8" aria-labelledby="p4">
        <h2 id="p4" class="text-3xl font-bold">IV. The silent seller</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed !text-[#cbd6cd]">
          The mishna dealt with an animal bought from a gentile. Now a Jew buys a cow from a <em>Jew</em>, and the seller says
          nothing about whether she has given birth before. Her next male calf: firstborn or not (21b:6–7)? For each Amora,
          fill in the seller's thought bubble, then rule on the calf.
        </p>
        <div id="sellers" class="mt-5 space-y-5"></div>
        <div id="duty" class="mt-5 space-y-5"></div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ Part V: clot ============ -->
      <section class="mt-12 border-t border-[#2a3a32] pt-8" aria-labelledby="p5">
        <h2 id="p5" class="text-3xl font-bold">V. The clot in the field</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed !text-[#cbd6cd]" dir="rtl" lang="he">
          רַבִּי אֱלִיעֶזֶר בֶּן יַעֲקֹב אוֹמֵר: בְּהֵמָה גַּסָּה שֶׁשָּׁפְעָה חֲרָרַת דָּם…
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed !text-[#cbd6cd]">
          The new mishna (21b:9): a large animal expelled a mass of congealed blood. Perhaps a male fetus was in there.
        </p>
        <div id="clot" class="mt-5 space-y-5"></div>
        <div id="final" class="mt-6"></div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ Learn ============ -->
      <section class="mt-12 border-t border-[#2a3a32] pt-8" aria-labelledby="learn">
        <h2 id="learn" class="text-3xl font-bold">Learn the real daf</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed !text-[#cbd6cd]">
          Bekhorot 21 opens by closing out yesterday's question: even if a goat can recover from a <em>tinuf</em> and give birth within
          her year, one that actually gave birth to a live kid cannot (21a:1). Then comes Rabbi Shimon's kid and the four readings, the
          firstborn-or-sacrifice analogy with its mnemonics, the shepherds' word for a <em>tinuf</em>, Rav Ḥisda's unanswered question,
          the silent seller, and Rabbi Eliezer ben Ya'akov's mishna. Rashi spells out each mnemonic word; Rabbeinu Gershom works the
          calendar of 21a day by day, and Rashi offers two readings of it.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2 text-sm">
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.21a" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#e3ae5c]/50 px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#e3ae5c] hover:border-[#e3ae5c]">Bekhorot 21 on Sefaria ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Rabbeinu_Gershom_on_Bekhorot.21a" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#2a3a32] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#94a69c] hover:border-[#e3ae5c]">Rabbeinu Gershom ×34 ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Bekhorot.21a" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#2a3a32] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#94a69c] hover:border-[#e3ae5c]">Rashi ×29 ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Steinsaltz_on_Bekhorot.21a" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#2a3a32] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#94a69c] hover:border-[#e3ae5c]">Steinsaltz ×15 ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Bekhorot.21a.1.1" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#2a3a32] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#94a69c] hover:border-[#e3ae5c]">Tosafot ×11 ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chidushei_Halachot_on_Bekhorot.21a" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#2a3a32] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#94a69c] hover:border-[#e3ae5c]">Maharsha, Chidushei Halachot ×8 ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Rashash_on_Bekhorot.21a" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#2a3a32] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#94a69c] hover:border-[#e3ae5c]">Rashash ×8 ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.83a" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#2a3a32] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#94a69c] hover:border-[#e3ae5c]">Chullin 83a: the four announced days ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.22a.1" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#2a3a32] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#94a69c] hover:border-[#e3ae5c]">Continue: Bekhorot 22a ↗</a>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-6 text-sm !text-[#6f8277]">
          Part of the <a href="/daf" class="underline decoration-[#35473e] hover:!text-[#94a69c]">Daf Yomi Arcade</a>,
          a new game from every daf. Texts and links via the Sefaria API.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>

  <style is:global>
    .frank { font-family: 'Frank Ruhl Libre', Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif; }
    .opt, .act, .gate {
      border-radius: 0.4rem;
      border: 1px solid #3f5448;
      background: #0f1613;
      color: #e6ece4;
      padding: 0.5rem 0.9rem;
      font-size: 1rem;
      text-align: left;
      transition: border-color 0.15s, background-color 0.15s;
    }
    .opt:hover:not(:disabled), .act:hover:not(:disabled), .gate:hover:not(:disabled) { border-color: #e3ae5c; }
    .opt:focus-visible, .act:focus-visible, .gate:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #e3ae5c; outline-offset: 2px; }
    .opt:disabled, .act:disabled { opacity: 0.55; cursor: default; }
    .gate { min-height: 5.5rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.25rem; }
    .gate[data-state='shimon'] { border-color: #e3ae5c; background: #2b2213; }
    .gate[data-state='shut'] { border-style: dashed; opacity: 0.6; background: #1a1414; }
    .gate[data-state='open'] { border-color: #7fc4b0; background: #13241f; opacity: 0.8; }
    .ok { border-color: #8fca9a !important; background: #15291b !important; opacity: 1 !important; }
    .bad { border-color: #c4553f !important; background: #2c1714 !important; opacity: 1 !important; }
    .card { border-radius: 0.5rem; border: 1px solid #2a3a32; background: #16201b; padding: 1rem; }
    .knot { transition: transform 0.5s ease-out; }
    .drop { animation: drop 0.45s ease-out; }
    @keyframes drop { from { transform: translateY(-12px); opacity: 0; } to { transform: none; opacity: 1; } }
    .crack { animation: crack 0.4s; }
    @keyframes crack { 25% { transform: translateX(-5px); } 75% { transform: translateX(5px); } }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      .opt, .act, .gate, .knot { transition: none !important; }
      .drop, .crack { animation: none !important; }
    }
  </style>

  <script>
    const $ = (id: string) => document.getElementById(id)!;
    const sef = (ref: string) => `https://www.sefaria.org/${ref.replace(/ (\d+[ab]?):/, '.$1.').replace(/ /g, '_')}`;
    const link = (ref: string) =>
      `<a href="${sef(ref)}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="!text-[#e3ae5c] underline decoration-[#35473e] hover:!text-[#f2cf93]">${ref} ↗</a>`;
    const good = (s: string) => `<p class="!text-[#b9e2c0]">✓ ${s}</p>`;
    const miss = (s: string) => `<p class="!text-[#f0bfb3]">✗ ${s}</p>`;
    const note = (s: string) => `<p class="!text-[#cbd6cd]">${s}</p>`;
    const score: Record<string, [number, number]> = { gates: [0, 5], tug: [0, 11], shep: [0, 4], seller: [0, 7], clot: [0, 3] };
    let finalShown = false;
    const tally = () => {
      const got = Object.values(score).reduce((a, [g]) => a + g, 0);
      const max = Object.values(score).reduce((a, [, m]) => a + m, 0);
      $('tally').innerHTML = `<span class="!text-[#e3ae5c] font-bold">${got} / ${max}</span>`;
      if (finalShown) {
        const rank = got >= max - 3 ? 'a wise shepherd, the kind the Sages send for' : got >= max / 2 ? 'a buyer who remembers to ask' : 'still waiting outside the pen';
        $('final').innerHTML = `<div class="card text-center"><p class="text-sm !text-[#94a69c]">Final score</p>
          <p class="text-4xl font-black !text-[#e3ae5c]">${got} / ${max}</p><p class="mt-1 !text-[#cbd6cd]">Ranked: ${rank}.</p></div>`;
      }
    };
    tally();

    type Q = { q: string; opts: string[]; ans: number; why: string; ref: string };
    const ask = (host: HTMLElement, item: Q, bucket: string, after?: (right: boolean) => void) => {
      const div = document.createElement('div');
      div.className = 'card drop';
      div.innerHTML = `<p class="!text-[#e6ece4]">${item.q}</p><div class="mt-2 flex flex-col gap-1.5">${item.opts
        .map((o, j) => `<button class="opt text-sm" data-j="${j}">${o}</button>`)
        .join('')}</div><div class="out mt-2 space-y-1 text-sm" aria-live="polite"></div>`;
      host.appendChild(div);
      div.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('button.opt').forEach((b) =>
        b.addEventListener('click', () => {
          const right = +b.dataset.j! === item.ans;
          div.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('button.opt').forEach((x) => {
            x.disabled = true;
            if (+x.dataset.j! === item.ans) x.classList.add('ok');
          });
          if (!right) { b.classList.add('bad'); div.classList.add('crack'); }
          else score[bucket][0]++;
          div.querySelector('.out')!.innerHTML = (right ? good(item.why) : miss(item.why)) + note(link(item.ref));
          tally();
          after?.(right);
        }),
      );
      return div;
    };
    const seq = (host: HTMLElement, items: Q[], bucket: string, done?: () => void) => {
      const step = (i: number) => {
        if (i >= items.length) return done?.();
        ask(host, items[i], bucket, () => step(i + 1));
      };
      step(0);
    };

    // ================= Part I: four gates =================
    const GATES = [
      { name: "Ze'eiri's thirty days", sub: 'After a tinuf, no pregnancy for 30 days', shimon: 'Rabbi Shimon rejects it: they can conceive in month seven and give birth in the last month of year one.' },
      { name: 'Incomplete months', sub: 'Can she give birth before full months?', shimon: 'Rabbi Shimon: she can give birth after incomplete months.' },
      { name: 'Part of a day', sub: 'Does part of a day count as a whole day?', shimon: 'Rabbi Shimon: part of the day is like the whole day, so she can give birth on the last day of year one.' },
      { name: 'Before its time', sub: 'Does a kid under 8 days enter the pen?', shimon: 'Rabbi Shimon: a kid "lacking time" enters the pen to be tithed.' },
    ];
    // state per gate: '' untouched, 'shimon' disputed now, 'shut' agreed shut, 'open' agreed open
    const gstate = ['', '', '', ''];
    const ROUNDS = [
      { clue: 'אִיכָּא בֵּינַיְיהוּ דִּזְעֵירִי… תַּנָּא קַמָּא אִית לֵיהּ דִּזְעֵירִי, וְרַבִּי שִׁמְעוֹן לֵית לֵיהּ', ans: 0, prev: -1, prevTo: '', ref: 'Bekhorot 21a:2' },
      { clue: 'דְּכוּלֵּי עָלְמָא אִית לְהוּ דִּזְעֵירִי, וְהָכָא בְּיוֹלֶדֶת לִמְקוּטָּעִין קָא מִיפַּלְגִי', ans: 1, prev: 0, prevTo: 'shut', ref: 'Bekhorot 21a:3' },
      { clue: 'דְּכוּלֵּי עָלְמָא אֵינָהּ יוֹלֶדֶת לִמְקוּטָּעִין, וְהָכָא בְּמִקְצָת הַיּוֹם כְּכוּלּוֹ קָמִיפַּלְגִי', ans: 2, prev: 1, prevTo: 'shut', ref: 'Bekhorot 21a:4' },
      { clue: 'דְּכוּלֵּי עָלְמָא אָמְרִינַן מִקְצָת הַיּוֹם כְּכוּלּוֹ, וְהָכָא בִּמְחוּסַּר זְמַן נִכְנָס לַדִּיר לְהִתְעַשֵּׂר קָמִיפַּלְגִי', ans: 3, prev: 2, prevTo: 'open', ref: 'Bekhorot 21a:5' },
    ];
    const LABEL: Record<string, string> = { '': '', shimon: 'disputed: Rabbi Shimon opens', shut: 'agreed: shut for both', open: 'agreed: open for both' };
    let gRound = 0;
    const drawGates = () => {
      $('gateboard').innerHTML = GATES.map(
        (g, i) => `<button class="gate text-sm" data-i="${i}" data-state="${gstate[i]}" aria-label="${g.name}. ${LABEL[gstate[i]]}">
          <span class="font-bold !text-[#e6ece4]">${['א', 'ב', 'ג', 'ד'][i]}. ${g.name}</span>
          <span class="text-xs !text-[#94a69c]">${g.sub}</span>
          <span class="mt-auto text-xs font-bold ${gstate[i] === 'shimon' ? '!text-[#e3ae5c]' : gstate[i] === 'open' ? '!text-[#7fc4b0]' : '!text-[#c98a7d]'}">${LABEL[gstate[i]]}</span>
        </button>`,
      ).join('');
      $('gateboard').querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.gate').forEach((b) => b.addEventListener('click', () => pickGate(+b.dataset.i!)));
    };
    let gCard: HTMLElement | null = null;
    let gTried = false;
    const showRound = () => {
      if (gRound >= ROUNDS.length) return gatesDone();
      const r = ROUNDS[gRound];
      gTried = false;
      gCard = document.createElement('div');
      gCard.className = 'card drop';
      gCard.innerHTML = `<p class="text-sm !text-[#94a69c]">Reading ${gRound + 1} of 4${gRound ? ': "And if you wish, say…"' : ''}</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-xl leading-relaxed !text-[#e6ece4]" dir="rtl" lang="he">${r.clue}</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm !text-[#cbd6cd]">Tap the gate this reading puts in dispute on the board above.</p>
        <div class="out mt-2 space-y-1 text-sm" aria-live="polite"></div>`;
      $('gates').appendChild(gCard);
    };
    const pickGate = (i: number) => {
      if (!gCard || gRound >= ROUNDS.length) return;
      const r = ROUNDS[gRound];
      const out = gCard.querySelector('.out')!;
      if (gstate[i] === 'shut' || gstate[i] === 'open') {
        out.innerHTML = note(`That gate is already agreed on. Both sides hold the same there now.`);
        return;
      }
      if (i !== r.ans) {
        gTried = true;
        gCard.classList.remove('crack'); void gCard.offsetWidth; gCard.classList.add('crack');
        out.innerHTML = miss(`Not that one. Look for the key phrase after וְהָכָא… or the name in the line.`);
        return;
      }
      if (!gTried) score.gates[0]++;
      if (r.prev >= 0) gstate[r.prev] = r.prevTo;
      gstate[i] = 'shimon';
      let extra = '';
      if (r.prevTo === 'shut') extra = ` The previous gate is now <strong>shut for both</strong>: everyone accepts the stricter view there.`;
      if (r.prevTo === 'open') extra = ` Notice the twist: the previous gate is now <strong>open for both</strong>. Everyone says part of a day is like the whole day, so the kid can be born on the last day of the year. The fight moves to whether that newborn, under eight days old, may enter the pen at all.`;
      out.innerHTML = good(`${GATES[i].shimon} The first tanna keeps it shut.${extra}`) + note(link(r.ref));
      tally();
      gRound++;
      drawGates();
      showRound();
    };
    const gatesDone = () => {
      ask($('gates'), {
        q: 'One of the four readings has a baraita behind it, quoting Rabbi Shimon by name. Which gate does it confirm?',
        opts: ["Ze'eiri's thirty days", 'Incomplete months', 'Part of a day', 'Before its time: a kid under eight days enters the pen'],
        ans: 3,
        why: 'Rabbi Shimon ben Yehuda in the name of Rabbi Shimon: a kid lacking time enters the pen to be tithed, "and they are like a firstborn: holy before its time and offered after its time." Which raises the question in Part II.',
        ref: 'Bekhorot 21b:1',
      }, 'gates');
    };
    drawGates();
    showRound();

    // ================= Part II: tug of war =================
    type Tile = { he: string; en: string; side: 'b' | 'k' | 'x'; why: string };
    const TILES: Tile[] = [
      { he: 'גּוֹאֵל', en: 'Not redeemed, even once blemished', side: 'b', why: 'Firstborn: "you shall not redeem" (Num. 18:17); tithe: "it shall not be redeemed" (Lev. 27:33). Ordinary sacrifices are redeemed when blemished.' },
      { he: 'מוּם', en: 'A prior blemish doesn’t stop them becoming fully holy', side: 'b', why: 'Rashi: a firstborn or tithe animal born blemished is still fully holy; a blemished animal consecrated as a sacrifice is not (14a).' },
      { he: 'תְּמוּרָה', en: 'A substitute for them is not offered', side: 'b', why: 'Rashi: their temura is not sacrificed, unlike the temura of other offerings.' },
      { he: 'אֲכִילָה', en: 'Eaten in their blemish without redemption', side: 'b', why: 'Rashi: firstborn eaten by the kohen, tithe by the owner, both without redemption; other sacrifices must be redeemed first.' },
      { he: 'זָכָר', en: 'Not limited to males', side: 'k', why: 'Tithe and sacrifices can be female; only males are firstborn.' },
      { he: 'קָדוֹשׁ', en: 'Made holy by a person, not holy from the womb', side: 'k', why: 'Tithe is sanctified by counting under the rod, sacrifices by consecration; a firstborn is holy from birth.' },
      { he: 'בְּמַתָּנוֹת', en: 'Not one of the priestly gifts', side: 'k', why: 'The firstborn goes to the kohen; tithe and peace offerings are eaten by the owners (Rashi).' },
      { he: 'פָּשׁוּט', en: 'An ordinary animal, not a first one', side: 'k', why: 'Tithe and sacrifices apply to any animal; firstborn status needs the first to open the womb.' },
      { he: '✗', en: 'Both may be consecrated before eight days old', side: 'x', why: 'That’s the very question being asked about the tithe. You can’t use the conclusion as a point of comparison.' },
      { he: '✗', en: 'Both are eaten only by kohanim', side: 'x', why: 'Not true of the tithe: the owners eat it. (Only the firstborn goes to the kohen.)' },
    ];
    const order = TILES.map((_, i) => i).sort(() => Math.random() - 0.5);
    let pull = 0, placed = 0, bPts = 0, kPts = 0;
    const moveKnot = () => {
      $('knot').style.transform = `translateX(${Math.max(-150, Math.min(150, pull * 34))}px)`;
      $('tugcount').textContent = `Firstborn ${bPts} · Sacrifices ${kPts} · ${TILES.length - placed} tiles left`;
    };
    moveKnot();
    order.forEach((ti) => {
      const t = TILES[ti];
      const row = document.createElement('div');
      row.className = 'card';
      row.innerHTML = `<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
          <span class="text-2xl font-bold !text-[#e6ece4] min-w-[5.5rem]" dir="rtl" lang="he">${t.he}</span>
          <span class="flex-1 min-w-[12rem] !text-[#cbd6cd]">${t.en}</span>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap gap-1.5">
          <button class="opt text-sm" data-s="b">← Firstborn</button>
          <button class="opt text-sm" data-s="k">Sacrifices →</button>
          <button class="opt text-sm" data-s="x">Not true / doesn't count</button>
        </div><div class="out mt-2 text-sm" aria-live="polite"></div>`;
      $('tiles').appendChild(row);
      row.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('button').forEach((b) =>
        b.addEventListener('click', () => {
          const right = b.dataset.s === t.side;
          row.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('button').forEach((x) => {
            x.disabled = true;
            if (x.dataset.s === t.side) x.classList.add('ok');
          });
          if (right) score.tug[0]++; else { b.classList.add('bad'); row.classList.add('crack'); }
          if (t.side === 'b') { pull--; bPts++; }
          if (t.side === 'k') { pull++; kPts++; }
          placed++;
          moveKnot();
          row.querySelector('.out')!.innerHTML = right ? good(t.why) : miss(t.why);
          tally();
          if (placed === TILES.length) tugDone();
        }),
      );
    });
    const tugDone = () => {
      const d = document.createElement('div');
      d.className = 'card drop';
      d.innerHTML = note(`<strong>Four against four.</strong> <span dir="rtl" lang="he">גּוֹאֵל, מוּם, תְּמוּרַת, אֲכִילָה</span> pulls toward the firstborn; <span dir="rtl" lang="he">זָכָר, קָדוֹשׁ, בְּמַתָּנוֹת, פָּשׁוּט</span> pulls right back: "On the contrary!" The rope doesn't move. Neither analogy wins on logic. ${link('Bekhorot 21b:2-3')}`);
      $('bridge').appendChild(d);
      ask($('bridge'), {
        q: 'So the Gemara drops the logic and says Rabbi Shimon learned it from a <em>gezera shava</em>, a shared word. Which pair of verses ties the tithe to the firstborn?',
        opts: [
          '<span dir="rtl" lang="he">וְהַעֲבַרְתָּ כָל פֶּטֶר רֶחֶם</span> (Ex. 13:12) ↔ <span dir="rtl" lang="he">כֹּל אֲשֶׁר יַעֲבֹר תַּחַת הַשָּׁבֶט</span> (Lev. 27:32)',
          '<span dir="rtl" lang="he">וּמִיּוֹם הַשְּׁמִינִי וָהָלְאָה יֵרָצֶה</span> (Lev. 22:27) ↔ <span dir="rtl" lang="he">כֹּל אֲשֶׁר יַעֲבֹר תַּחַת הַשָּׁבֶט</span> (Lev. 27:32)',
          '<span dir="rtl" lang="he">לֹא תִפְדֶּה</span> (Num. 18:17) ↔ <span dir="rtl" lang="he">לֹא יִגָּאֵל</span> (Lev. 27:33)',
        ],
        ans: 0,
        why: 'הַעֲבָרָה הַעֲבָרָה: "you shall pass" over every firstborn, and everything that "passes" under the rod. The verbal link wins where the tug-of-war tied, so the tithe is holy before its time like a firstborn. (Lev. 22:27 is the eighth-day rule for sacrifices, per Rashi: the source for the other side.)',
        ref: 'Bekhorot 21b:3',
      }, 'tug');
    };

    // ================= Part III: shepherd =================
    seq($('shep'), [
      {
        q: 'Rava quotes the shepherds: <span dir="rtl" lang="he">דְּצָלְתָּא אֲצַר חֵיוְתָא</span>. What does a tinuf look like according to Rava, and according to Shmuel?',
        opts: [
          'Rava: a murky discharge of a fetus the womb held back. Shmuel: bubbles of blood.',
          'Rava: bubbles of blood. Shmuel: a murky discharge.',
          'Both: a fully formed fetus the size of a bean.',
        ],
        ans: 0,
        why: 'Rava, in the shepherds’ own words: murky stuff, a fetus the womb held in (Rashi: the fetus dissolved). Shmuel: <span dir="rtl" lang="he">בַּעְבּוּעֵי דִּדְמָא</span>, bubbles of blood.',
        ref: 'Bekhorot 21b:4',
      },
      {
        q: 'And one must show it to a <em>ḥakham</em>. "A ḥakham? How would he know?" Who is the right expert, according to Rav Pappa?',
        opts: ['The head of the court', 'A physician', 'A wise shepherd (<span dir="rtl" lang="he">רוֹעֶה חָכָם</span>)', 'The animal’s owner'],
        ans: 2,
        why: 'Rav Pappa: a wise shepherd, who knows the different discharges an animal produces. Expertise beats title.',
        ref: 'Bekhorot 21b:4',
      },
      {
        q: 'Rav Ḥisda: in a woman, a fetus forms in forty days. In an animal, how many? Rav Pappa offers Ze\'eiri: "no tinuf in less than thirty days". Does that settle it?',
        opts: [
          'Yes: thirty days in an animal',
          'No: Ze\'eiri was talking about the thirty days after a tinuf when she won’t accept a male',
          'No: Ze\'eiri was talking about women',
        ],
        ans: 1,
        why: '<span dir="rtl" lang="he">הַהוּא לְקַבֵּל אִיתְּמַר</span>: that was said about receptivity after a tinuf, not about how long a fetus takes to form.',
        ref: 'Bekhorot 21b:5',
      },
      {
        q: 'So what is the answer to Rav Ḥisda’s question?',
        opts: ['Forty days, like a woman', 'Thirty days', 'The Gemara leaves it unresolved'],
        ans: 2,
        why: 'The question stays open. Even a wise shepherd can’t count it for you.',
        ref: 'Bekhorot 21b:5',
      },
    ], 'shep');

    // ================= Part IV: silent seller =================
    const THOUGHTS = [
      '“If she had already given birth, I’d brag about it: no calf to hand the kohen!”',
      '“He’s buying her for slaughter. Why would I mention her birth history?”',
      '“If she had never given birth, I’d have to warn him: there’s a prohibition at stake.”',
    ];
    const VERDICTS = ['Definitely a firstborn', 'Possibly a firstborn', 'Definitely not sacred'];
    const SAGES = [
      { name: 'Rav', t: 0, v: 0, ref: 'Bekhorot 21b:6', why: 'Rav: had she given birth, the seller would have bragged. He didn’t, so she hadn’t: <span dir="rtl" lang="he">בְּכוֹר וַדַּאי</span>.' },
      { name: 'Shmuel', t: 1, v: 1, ref: 'Bekhorot 21b:7', why: 'Shmuel: the seller assumes it’s for slaughter, so his silence tells us nothing: <span dir="rtl" lang="he">בְּכוֹר סָפֵק</span>.' },
      { name: 'Rabbi Yoḥanan', t: 2, v: 2, ref: 'Bekhorot 21b:7', why: 'Rabbi Yoḥanan: had she not given birth, a prohibition is at stake and he would have said so. He didn’t, so she had: <span dir="rtl" lang="he">חוּלִּין וַדָּאִין</span>.' },
    ];
    let sellersDone = 0;
    SAGES.forEach((s) => {
      const d = document.createElement('div');
      d.className = 'card';
      d.innerHTML = `<div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" class="h-10 w-10 shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="20" cy="14" r="8" fill="#5f7a6b"/><path d="M6 38 Q20 20 34 38" fill="#5f7a6b"/><path d="M15 16 h10" stroke="#0f1613" stroke-width="2"/></svg>
          <p class="text-xl font-bold !text-[#e6ece4]">${s.name}</p>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm !text-[#94a69c]">What does ${s.name} think is going on in the seller's head?</p>
        <div class="th mt-1 flex flex-col gap-1.5">${THOUGHTS.map((t, j) => `<button class="opt text-sm" data-j="${j}">💭 ${t}</button>`).join('')}</div>
        <div class="vd mt-3 hidden"><p class="text-sm !text-[#94a69c]">So the cow's next male calf is…</p>
        <div class="mt-1 flex flex-wrap gap-1.5">${VERDICTS.map((t, j) => `<button class="opt text-sm" data-j="${j}">${t}</button>`).join('')}</div></div>
        <div class="out mt-2 space-y-1 text-sm" aria-live="polite"></div>`;
      $('sellers').appendChild(d);
      const wire = (sel: string, ans: number, next: () => void) =>
        d.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>(`${sel} button`).forEach((b) =>
          b.addEventListener('click', () => {
            const right = +b.dataset.j! === ans;
            d.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>(`${sel} button`).forEach((x) => {
              x.disabled = true;
              if (+x.dataset.j! === ans) x.classList.add('ok');
            });
            if (right) score.seller[0]++; else { b.classList.add('bad'); d.classList.remove('crack'); void d.offsetWidth; d.classList.add('crack'); }
            tally();
            next();
          }),
        );
      wire('.th', s.t, () => d.querySelector('.vd')!.classList.remove('hidden'));
      wire('.vd', s.v, () => {
        d.querySelector('.out')!.innerHTML = note(s.why) + note(link(s.ref));
        if (++sellersDone === SAGES.length) dutyRound();
      });
    });
    const dutyRound = () => {
      ask($('duty'), {
        q: 'A baraita backs Rabbi Yoḥanan: on the days a seller must announce "I sold the mother today for slaughter", if he didn’t, the buyer may go ahead and slaughter the calf. Is that a refutation of Rav and Shmuel?',
        opts: [
          'Yes: silence means "nothing to report", so Rav and Shmuel fall',
          'No: there the Torah puts the duty on the seller; here it is on the buyer',
        ],
        ans: 1,
        why: '<span dir="rtl" lang="he">הָתָם בְּמוֹכֵר תַּלְיָא מִילְּתָא, הָכָא בְּלוֹקֵחַ תַּלְיָא מִילְּתָא</span>. With "it and its young", the seller must announce (Rashi, citing Chullin 83). With a firstborn, the owner of the herd must separate his own firstborns (Rashi: "of your herd and your flock", Deut. 15:19), so the buyer should have asked.',
        ref: 'Bekhorot 21b:8',
      }, 'seller');
    };

    // ================= Part V: clot =================
    seq($('clot'), [
      {
        q: 'Rabbi Eliezer ben Ya’akov: what happens to the clot, and to the mother?',
        opts: [
          'Given to the kohen; the mother’s next calf is still a firstborn',
          'Buried; the mother is exempt from the firstborn from now on',
          'Thrown out; nothing changes',
        ],
        ans: 1,
        why: '<span dir="rtl" lang="he">הֲרֵי זוֹ תִּקָּבֵר, וּפְטוּרָה מִן הַבְּכוֹרָה</span>. Perhaps there was a male in it that became holy as a firstborn when it came out, and it already opened the womb.',
        ref: 'Bekhorot 21b:9',
      },
      {
        q: 'Rabbi Ḥiyya teaches about the clot: does it impart impurity like a carcass, by touching or carrying?',
        opts: ['Yes, by both', 'By touching only', 'Neither by touching nor by carrying'],
        ans: 2,
        why: '<span dir="rtl" lang="he">אֵינָהּ מְטַמְּאָה לֹא בְּמַגָּע וְלֹא בְּמַשָּׂא</span>. And the Gemara pounces: if it isn’t treated as a fetus, why bury it?',
        ref: 'Bekhorot 21b:10',
      },
      {
        q: 'The daf ends on that question. Turn the page: why bury it?',
        opts: [
          'To publicize that the mother is exempt from the firstborn',
          'Because it is holy as a firstborn and may not be used',
          'So nobody becomes impure from it',
        ],
        ans: 0,
        why: 'Bekhorot 22a: the burial is a public sign, so people will know her next calf isn’t a firstborn. And why no impurity if it’s a real offspring? Rabbi Yoḥanan: the fetus is nullified in the majority of the blood around it.',
        ref: 'Bekhorot 22a:1',
      },
    ], 'clot', () => {
      finalShown = true;
      tally();
    });
  </script>
</Layout>
